 "derived_from": [],
 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Stella has a home business selling gourmet pizzas. The equation <span data-math=\"C = 4p + 25\">C = 4p + 25</span> models the relation between her weekly cost, <span data-math=\"C\">C</span>, in dollars and the number of pizzas, <span data-math=\"p\">p</span>, that she sells.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511336,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find Stella’s cost for a week when she sells no pizzas.\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"C = 4p + 25\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"C = 4\\left( 0 \\right) + 25 = 25\"></span></p>\n<p>Stella’s costs are $25 when no pizzas are sold.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$25"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511337,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the cost for a week when she sells 15 pizzas.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"C = 4\\left( {15} \\right) + 25 = 60 + 25 = 85\"></span></p>\n<p>Stella’s costs are $85.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$85"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511338,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Interpret the slope and <span data-math=\"C\">C</span>-intercept of the equation.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>When the equation is in the slope-intercept form of the equation of the line,</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y = mx + b\"></span>.</p>\n<p><i>m</i> = the slope.</p>\n<p>(0, <i>b</i>) = the y-intercept.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"C = 4p + 25\"></span></p>\n<p>The <i>y</i>-intercept gives the cost when no pizzas are sold: $25.</p>\n<p>The slope gives the rate at which costs increase per pizza made. For every pizza sold, Stella’s costs increase by $4.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The slope, 4, means that the weekly cost, <span data-math=\"C\">C</span>, increases by $4 when the number of pizzas sold, <span data-math=\"p\">p</span>, increases by 1. The <span data-math=\"C\">C</span>-intercept means that when the number of pizzas sold is 0, the weekly cost is $25."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511339,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Graph the equation.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Plot the point (0, 25).</p>\n<p>From that point, use the slope <span data-math=\"\\left( {m = \\frac{{rise}}{{run}} = \\frac{4}{1}} \\right)\"></span> to go up 4, then right 1 to plot the next point.</p>\n<p>Connect the two points with a line.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Graph:\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBcU1QIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--a3acd3dd0c7e2ac50853093852723da54a9bdcfc/CS_Figure_05_08_030.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x-axis ranges from negative 60 to 210, in increments of 15. The y-axis ranges from negative 75 to 200, in increments of 15. The line passes through the points, (negative 15, negative 35), (0, 25), (13, 85), and (30, 145). Note: all values are approximate.\">"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
